      "writtenOn": "2025-07-22T02:47:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Initially I plan to use this as an option for the host to query the required memory size, like if host pass an INVALID_PAGE, then the pkvm return required memory size. But later seems this not necessary. As VALID_PAGE() check is harmless and can still prevent the host sending INVALID_PAGE, leave it as it is. Although it mostly used by the KVM MMU thing, there are still some other usages, like for the partition assist page in hv_get_partition_assist_page(), and for the snp_vmsa_gpa in sev_snp_ap_creation().\n\nAnd yes, I will add a TODO for this as well. Thanks!",
